.TH PING 8
.SH NAME
ping \- IPv4 network command
.SH SYNOPSIS
ping [-n] [-c count] [-i seconds] [-W seconds] [-s size] host
.SH DESCRIPTION
Send ICMP echo requests. Host names use resolver(3); replies show reverse names unless -n selects numeric output. Unknown names exit 2. The installed setuid command drops privilege after opening its raw socket, before resolving names.
